# .dockerignore - trim build-context bloat (refs #499).
#
# The only build whose context is the repo root (`docker build ... .`)
# is dockerfile/Dockerfile.test-tools, and it copies NOTHING from the
# context (every COPY is `COPY --from=<stage>`). Dockerfile.example is
# only ever built against a synthesized consumer repo (integration-e2e
# job copies the template into a temp repo's .base/ and builds there),
# never against base's own root. So nothing the root-context build
# needs is excluded below.
#
# We still KEEP the source/template trees (script/, test/, dist/config/,
# .base/, dockerfile/, Dockerfile, .hadolint.yaml, entrypoints) so this
# stays forward-safe: Dockerfile.example's lint/smoke stages COPY those
# paths, and the file doubles as the downstream template.

# ── VCS / repo metadata ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore

# ── Docs (no build COPYs them) ───────────────────────────────────────
doc/
README*
LICENSE

# ── CI / lint config not consumed by any root-context build ──────────
.github/
.codecov.yaml

# ── Derived / generated artifacts (see script/docker/lib/gitignore.sh
#    _canonical_gitignore_entries) ──────────────────────────────────
#
# A COPY OF A COMPUTED SET, AND GATED AS ONE (base#1275). Every line
# below is one entry of _canonical_dockerignore_entries, which delegates
# to _canonical_gitignore_entries, in that function's own order. The
# agreement is not remembered: `./script/test/test.sh
# --canonical-ignore-sync-only` derives both sides and fails naming any
# canonical entry this block lacks, so the next entry added to the
# function fails until this file agrees. Add new derived artifacts THERE,
# then re-run the gate and paste what it names.
#
# The gate is ONE-DIRECTIONAL: it asks that every canonical entry be
# here, and allows extras. That is what _sync_dockerignore does for a
# consumer, and it is what lets the base-local section below exist.
# Presence is a WHOLE LINE -- the `*.bak` glob below would cover three of
# these in effect, and they are listed here anyway, because `grep -qxF`
# is the test the shipped sync applies and it would append them verbatim
# regardless.
.env
.env.local
.env.local.toml
.env.generated
.env.bak
.env.local.bak
env.local.toml
compose.yaml
.setup.conf.bak
setup.toml.bak
.setup.conf.local
.setup.conf.local.bak
setup.local.toml
coverage/
.Dockerfile.generated
.docker.xauth
log/
/deploy/

# ── Derived artifacts that are base's OWN, not the canonical set ─────
#
# Below the managed block on purpose: the header above claims its lines
# come from the shipped function, and these do not. `.prev-release/` is
# the released-tree scratch script/test/prepare-prev-release.sh
# materialises for the vendored-drift checks; nothing in dist/ names it,
# and base's root .gitignore documents it as base's own. It sat inside
# the block until base#1275 -- correct content under a false header.
#
# `runtime.env` used to sit there too and is now GONE rather than moved:
# it names a retired artifact (dist/script/docker/lib/setup_cmd.sh
# records "S7: runtime.env retired"), so a reader of the block concluded
# the template still emits it.
.prev-release/

# ── Editor / OS / backup cruft ───────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ── Local Claude Code session state ──────────────────────────────────
.claude
CLAUDE.md
